Started a game up as a Dwarven Valkyrie.

Found a few random fountains early, #dip'ed into them for Excalibur.
Good plan, right?  Well, yeah, except nobody told me you had to be
level 5 to actually get Excal. On the other hand, getting a pair of
water demons, the second of which gives you a wish, makes up for it.
Right?

Q - a blessed +2 silver dragon scale mail (being worn)

After Elbereth'ing and fleeing to the downstairs of the Gnomish Mines,
I headed for Minetown with my pet dog.

I made it to Minetown, but my dog did not, refusing to cross a magic
trap.  Went down to the next level, tamed a f, had it kill a couple
gnomes for a pickaxe, then went to get my dog. After doing some
stealing, I noticed that I was XL1 still, so spent all my money on
protection, got my AC down by 8 or so, had negative AC at that point.
After doing that and stealing some good stuff, I thought it was a good
plan to read a spellbook in a shop... we all know how that goes.
Fortunately, the Keystone Kops couldn't really hurt me, and I killed
them all and leveled up a decent amount.  After this, I decided to go
to the main branch to Sokoban (did the usual oracularities)- got a ton
of food, a few wands, and... an Amulet of Reflection.

A bit redundant, but might as well wear it anyway.  At this point I've
got a =oSD as well, and decided to dive down, since I was too low for
the Quest...
A couple of coaligned altars along the way, and I've got Mjollnir as
well as Excalibur.

Upon reaching Medusa, I realized I lacked a way to cross the water, so
i elected to zap a /oDig down, and go straight to the castle.  A bit of
a belated DfV, but it works.

The drawbridge did its usual job, and I killed Xorns with Mojo.
Getting in the castle was rather fun, as I sat on the throne and
summoned 4 Dragons (Black, Red, Green, Blue). Oops. Elbereth and a
=oConflict later, and I feel firm.

After killing some of the soldiers, I fiddle with my weaponry, and
#twoweapon between Mjollnir and a Silver Saber.

A little bit more fighting, I get the wand of wishing, and start
setting up the AK.

Highlights:
  Y - a blessed fireproof +2 cloak of magic resistance
  Z - a blessed rustproof +2 pair of gauntlets of power
  c - a blessed fireproof +2 pair of speed boots
  a - the blessed rustproof +2 Frost Brand
  h - a blessed bag of holding
  2 Blessed Scrolls of Genocide also made an appearance, and went to ;
and L.

I turned to go back up to Medusa, dealt with all the stuff on the right
side, and then went to head to my quest.... then realized I had no way
to get across. Damn. Can't go up, so the only other option is to go
down.

And go down I did, all the way down to the Vibrating Square, mapping
out Gehennom, getting some uncursed Geno's (for MMF's and MF's, in that
order), and some rings, but not entering the Wizard's Tower or Vlad's
tower (indeed, I forgot to locate the second upstairs).  I sat in the
temple in the Valley of the Dead for a while trying to wear-ID a ring
of levitation that wasn't cursed, but to no avail. I did get some
protection, though.  Either it was cursed, or I didn't have it.  I went
up to Medusa again, and worked my way across with a wand of cold...
only to run out halfway across. Not to be set back here, I pulled out a
wand of Polymorph (engrave-testing is awesome) and polypiled a whole
stack of junk wands, hoping to get a wand of cold.  All my /oDig's
turned into an Iron golem, which was a minor annoyance, but I did get
across, and headed up to my Quest Level.  The Quest ended up being
fairly simple, though I did forget to grab the bell. Whoops. Had to go
back down.  #rode a baluchitherium, it starved rather quickly, and I
was quickly on foot again. Since I'm about to go to Gehennom again, I
started digging out the stair-to-stair paths, and while I was at it, I
stopped by Minetown.  Killed a few shopkeepers, killed the
cross-aligned priest (after getting more protection.. the very last one
failed due to being the 11th- so I got a refund), converted the altar,
dug out some stuff around it (but not the whole level), and set up a
pudding farm.  After an hour or so of offering the puddings, I decided
to just kill them for items and started pasting .         .
.              2 (etc) into the PUTTY window. After reaching about 6
million points, a random peaceful broke the wall behind me, so I
stopped farming, and just calmly read a blessed scroll of genocide on
P.  That cleared out the farm in a hurry, and I was left to just mop up
the remaining enemies.  After killing a few mobs and picking up the
goods, I had genocided around 40 monsters or so, as well as having
pretty much everything in the game ID'ed thanks to polypiling.  A bit
of poly'ing on potions resulted in me at level 30 with St:25 Dx:20
Co:20 In:16 Wi:16 Ch:16, and +6 Frost Brand and Silver Saber, as well
as -28 AC and a large complement of rings for all situations, as well
as multiple Amulets of Life Saving from a wand of wishing that was
handy.

Both Rodney and Vlad were pushovers, and the candles I got from
minetown way back when could finally serve their use.  I returned to
the Vibrating Square, and entered Moloch's Sanctum.

The zoo there was quite annoying, but was easily dealt with with   A -
an uncursed ring of conflict.
The High Priest of Moloch was a fairly simple fight, though the S's
constantly got in the way. I nearly forgot to actually grab the Amulet,
and was in fact halfway out of the Sanctum when I realized I was
forgetting something.

The 'mysterious force' is one of the worst things in gaming, a poorly
designed bad idea that serves no purpose but to annoy people.  Sending
someone backwards 5 levels completely randomly doesn't serve any real
purpose, and is just an irritant.  After dealing with that nonsense for
far longer than anyone should have to, I finally made it to the Planes.

I only have one scroll of gold detection, but pick up a second, so I
make it through Earth the hard way, wearing Levitation the whole time,
as preparation for the Air plane. Earth was simply tedious, with having
to switch from Frosty+SilverSaber to a rusty corroded pickaxe, but I
was never in any real danger of dying.

The Air Elementals on Air plane were annoying, but couldn't
consistently deal enough damage to bring me close to death, and so I
ended up on Water without doing much fighting. The portal was found
with the usual Confused ?oGD.

The Water Plane strategy was to just confuse, read a ?oGD, and levitate
to the general area. This worked well, and I was on Astral.
I forgot to take off Levitation for a while, but eventually remembered
to put Conflict on.  The first altar I chose to approach was the
central one, where Death resided.  This ended up not being aligned, and
Death was never an issue because I was able to keep him on the other
side of the snakes after a while.  I moved to the left altar, home of
Pestilence, and got ready by pulling a ton of K-Rations out of the bag
of holding.  As I approached the altar, a stroll of Stinking Cloud
helped soften the enemies up, and Pestilence ended up dying to a random
Dragon in the temple.  I walked to the high altar, and #offered Tyr the
Amulet of Yendor, ascending into demigoddess-hood.

